    "title": "Higley Center to host Mark Wood Trans-Siberian Experience - NewsBreak",
    "text": "16 hours ago\nThe Higley Center for the Performing Arts will present the Mark Wood Trans-Siberian Experience at 7 p.m. Saturday, Dec. 6.\nDoors open at 6 p.m. The event is a repeat of last year’s sold-out performance and features a holiday and year-round concert experience inspired by the music of Trans-Siberian Orchestra and Van Helsing’s Curse, along with classic rock favorites.\nWood, an electric violinist and Juilliard-trained musician, was a founding member of Trans-Siberian Orchestra and helped propel the group to multiplatinum success during its early years. He also performed as part of Van Helsing’s Curse, a theatrical rock project created by Dee Snider of Twisted Sister.\nJoining Wood on stage will be vocalist Laura Kaye, who has performed with artists including James Brown and Aretha Franklin.\nTickets are $30-$49.\n480-279-7194. higleycenter.org",
